.el .ds Aq '
.TH pidvault 1  "pidvault 0.3.1" 
.SH NAME
pidvault \- Per\-shell access to an encrypted SSH configuration directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpidvault\fR [\fB\-\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-mount\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Per\-shell access to an encrypted SSH configuration directory
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/pidvault.sock]
Daemon control socket
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-socket\fR \fI<AGENT_SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/pidvault\-agent.sock]
The agent that signs with vault keys
.TP
\fB\-\-mount\fR \fI<MOUNT>\fR [default: /run/pidvault]
Where the daemon mounts; each of your vaults is a directory inside it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pidvault\-daemon(1)
Serve the vaults (started by the systemd unit)
.TP
pidvault\-create(1)
Create a vault, empty or from a directory, and unlock it for the calling shell
.TP
pidvault\-unlock(1)
Give the calling shell and its descendants access to a vault
.TP
pidvault\-lock(1)
Revoke the calling shell\*(Aqs access to a vault, or to all of them
.TP
pidvault\-status(1)
Show your vaults; exit 0 if the calling shell has the vault (or any) unlocked
.TP
pidvault\-passwd(1)
Change the passphrase of a vault
.TP
pidvault\-export(1)
Write a vault, encrypted with its passphrase, to FILE (`\-` for stdout); needs the vault unlocked in the calling shell
.TP
pidvault\-import(1)
Make an exported vault yours and unlock it for the calling shell: on a new machine, or replacing one (which needs it unlocked, and is kept as a backup)
.TP
pidvault\-add\-key(1)
Copy a private key into a vault, removing its passphrase on the way; the vault must be unlocked in the calling shell
.TP
pidvault\-stub(1)
Print the lines to put at the top of ~/.ssh/config
.TP
pidvault\-shell\-init(1)
Print bash code that marks shells with a vault unlocked, in the prompt and the terminal title; use it with `eval "$(pidvault shell\-init)"` in ~/.bashrc
.TP
pidvault\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.3.1
